    "result_text": "Green. Here's what I did with the review.\n\n**Addressed \u2014 duplicated domain extraction (agreed).** I extracted a private `domainOf(String email)` helper in `OwnerEmail` that returns the lower-cased, trimmed domain (or `null` when there's no `@` or the domain is empty). Both `isDisposableDomain` and `isDisposableAdjacent` now call it, so the two blocklist checks share one definition of \"the domain of this address\" and can no longer drift. The previous inconsistency (trim/empty-guard in one but not the other) is resolved \u2014 both now use the trimmed form, which is harmless for the already-validated addresses these run against.\n\nOne thing the refactor surfaced: `DISPOSABLE_DOMAINS` is a `Set.of(...)`, whose `contains(null)` throws `NullPointerException`. The old `isDisposableDomain` never passed null (its `substring` result was always non-null), but `domainOf` can now return null, so I guarded the lookup with `domain != null && ...` to preserve the original \"absent domain \u2192 false\" behaviour.\n\n**Left as-is \u2014 precomputed base-label set (optional).** The reviewer flagged this as a judgment call, not required. With a three-entry blocklist the inline `substring` is negligible and keeps the adjacency rule readable in one place, so I kept it.\n\nFull suite passes (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`), so all acceptance behaviour is intact.",
